          "description": "Block until a condition is met or the timeout fires. \\\n                       Pass `selector` (CSS) to wait for an element; \\\n                       `condition: visible` (default for selectors) requires \\\n                       the element to be in the rendered tree, `condition: \\\n                       present` accepts any DOM match. Without a selector, \\\n                       `condition` may be `load` (`Page.loadEventFired`) or \\\n                       `networkidle` (500ms of network silence). Default \\\n                       timeout is 5000ms; capped at 120000ms.",
